{"name":"Morning Moor","hex":"#dad6ae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The early part of the day, especially from midnight to noon. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The early part of anything."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good morning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning"},{"term":"moor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extensive waste covered with patches of heath, and having a poor, light (and usually acidic) soil, but sometimes marshy, and abounding in peat; a heath.","A game preserve consisting of moorland."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cast anchor or become fastened.","To fix or secure (e.g. a vessel) in a particular place by casting anchor, or by fastening with ropes, cables or chains or the like."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/1280px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comet Ison at dawn, with Mercury at left","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComet_ison.jpg"}],"sounds":{"morning":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/En-uk-morning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b9/En-uk-morning.ogg/En-uk-morning.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-us-morning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En-us-morning.ogg/En-us-morning.ogg.mp3"}],"moor":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-moor.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-moor.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-moor.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-moor.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-moor.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/En-us-moor.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7b/En-us-moor.ogg/En-us-moor.ogg.mp3"}]}}}